        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0663" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Edward M. House Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-10">November 10,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. In view of the enormous claims which the French and Belgian Governments will
                    make on Germany I think we should get our engineers to make an approximate
                    estimate for our guidance. If you approve I can have this begun at once.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
